# Monitor profiles (legacy)

# These .lua files are no longer where layouts live. They are offered by
# `Monitor Profiles` (Quick Settings: SUPER SHIFT E, then Choose Monitor
# Profiles) as a ONE-WAY IMPORT: choosing one applies it and saves what is on
# screen as a layout under the same name, after which it restores automatically
# like any other layout.

# To make a layout now, use SUPER ALT D:
# - Arrange monitors - drag and drop (nwg-displays), or
# - Edit parameters (table)
# then Save current state as...

# tip: if you arrange monitors with nwg-displays, go through the SUPER ALT D
# menu rather than running it yourself. The menu is what applies the result and
# persists it. Running nwg-displays directly loses the arrangement, because this
# Lua config does not read the file it writes.

# Adding a file here still works as a way to get a profile in. The import writes
# the layout under the file's name, so give it a name you are happy to keep
# (letters, digits, space, dot, dash and underscore).
